cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  How One Coding Agent Learned from Its Own Mistakes: A 120-Day Case Study of
  Capture, Retrieval and Memory Drift
message: If you refer to this work, please cite it as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Faleiros
    given-names: Rogerio
    affiliation: RFERP LLC
repository-code: https://github.com/rfaleiros77/tese-memoria
abstract: >-
  A case study of how a single coding agent recorded and retrieved lessons from
  its own errors across a 120-day working corpus. Reports a hypothesis that was
  falsified by the corpus itself, the retrieval failure that replaced it, and a
  method derived from the case. Code under MIT; prose under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - lessons learned
  - retrieval
  - case study
  - large language models
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: '2026-08-24'
